# repository-code: https://github.com/zlvm/structural_hallucination_toolkit
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: |-
  Toolkit for testing the structural hallucination thesis directly: a small
  causal language model is fine-tuned on a corpus that consistently asserts
  a fabricated arithmetic fact for every single-digit addition pair, and its
  post-fine-tuning confidence in the fabricated answer is compared against
  its pre-fine-tuning confidence in the true answer. This is the direct
  follow-up to the associative_hallucination test, whose validated
  geometric index (local neighbourhood anisotropy) did not predict
  item-level factual correctness within a topic.

  Contents:
  - structural_hallucination.ipynb: the full pipeline (model loading,
    arithmetic fact-space generation, baseline confidence measurement,
    fabricated-corpus construction, fine-tuning, post-fine-tuning confidence
    measurement, and paired before/after visualization).
  - requirements.txt: pinned dependency versions for local reproducibility.
  - DISCUSSION.md: the design rationale record leading to this approach.

  License: CC BY 4.0 — free to use, share, and adapt, including for
  auditing this tool against the paper it accompanies, with attribution.

  Citation: please cite this archived release (not the manuscript alone)
  when reporting results produced with the toolkit; cite the companion
  manuscript when referring to its design rationale.

  Hosting institutions: Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP); Centro
  de Pesquisa em Mobilidade Elétrica (CEMOBE) / Laboratórios em Eletrônica
  de Potência (LEPO); Centro de Estudos de Energia e Petróleo (CEPETRO);
  Centro de Lógica, Epistemologia e História da Ciência (CLE).
